-- title:
--   Drinfeld chart over ramified constants at a Drinfeld-basis point
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $R$ be a Noetherian local ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_R$, which is regular with $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} R = 2$ and whose residue field is finite of characteristic $q$. Let $F$ be a commutative one-dimensional formal group law over $R$, and let $x_0, x_1 \in R$ be elements with $\mathfrak m_R = (x_0, x_1)$ such that $F$ satisfies `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic` for the ideal $\mathfrak m_R$, the prime $q$ and the pair $x_0, x_1$: taking $\mathfrak m_R$ as the defining ideal of the adic structure on $R$, there is a unit $u$ of $R[[T]]$ with $F.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,q = u \cdot F.\mathrm{drinfeldDivisor}\,q\,x_0\,x_1$. Let in addition $A$ be a discrete valuation ring (a domain) whose maximal ideal is generated by $\varpi$, let $\varepsilon \in A$ be a unit with $\varpi^{q-1} = \varepsilon \cdot q$, and let $\iota : A \to R$ be a local ring homomorphism. The assertion is that there exist a discrete valuation ring $W$ (a domain), complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W = (\sigma \varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0, X_1]]$ with $u$ and $v$ units and
--   $$f - (X_0 X_1^{\,q} - X_0^{\,q} X_1) \in (X_0, X_1)^{q+2},$$
--   and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e : R \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } W[[X_0, X_1]] \big/ \big( C(\sigma \varpi)\, v - f\, u \big)$$
--   such that $e(\iota a)$ is the class of the constant series $C(\sigma a)$ for every $a \in A$, and $e(x_0)$, $e(x_1)$ are the classes of $X_0$, $X_1$ respectively.
--
--   This is the local structure theorem for a point of Drinfeld level-$q$ structure at which the pair $x_0, x_1$ is a Drinfeld basis, in the form of Katz–Mazur's description of the completed local rings of the Drinfeld modular curve: the ring is a quotient of a two-variable power series ring over ramified constants by an equation congruent to $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo degree $q+2$, with the uniformiser $\varpi$ of the base discrete valuation ring appearing as $C(\sigma\varpi)v = fu$. Unlike earlier versions restricted to $q \ge 3$, it is stated for every prime $q$; it is used in the analysis of the completed stalks of a two-chart integral model of the full-level modular curve at supersingular points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_FormalGroup_IsDrinfeldBasisAdic_exists_ringEquiv_mvPowerSeries_quotient_drinfeldForm_of_isRegularLocalRing_of_prime.lean

